    "created_at": "2023-05-13T00:46:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-13T00:46:08Z",
    "body": "https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/7590/files#diff-d3ee5c059d6f87ae5944ee4d7e4a90b4ba229cb1adeb8a221831b27903bfd9d8R41 added a test assuming that video elements MUST have natural dimensions when video metadata but no frame is available because it waits for `loadedmetadata` rather than `canplay`.\r\n\r\nFirefox is the [only browser frequently failing](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/intrinsic_sizes.htm) [default object size after src is removed], but I have seen [a report of Safari failing](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1822382#c3).\r\n\r\nGecko uses container dimensions from metadata if available when it looks up natural dimensions, but does not necessarily re-trigger layout until HAVE_DATA (so there's obviously [a bug](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1832479) around there).\r\n\r\nA [timing-insensitive testcase](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/attachment.cgi?id=9333435) shows that Chrome gives the element natural dimensions from the container when no frame is available.  The testcase does not complete in Midori.",
