    "created_at": "2023-09-16T10:55:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-16T10:55:48Z",
    "body": "> > I'm not sure exactly what is meant by \"HAVE_METADATA but no video data has yet been obtained at all\" because HAVE_METADATA means that video dimensions are known.\r\n> \r\n> That would be if the video file's header has been decoded and the audio/video tracks and their properties are known, but no actual video frames have been decoded yet. But I'm not sure if any browsers currently handle this state, or if they actually always decode a frame to be certain about the video size.\r\n\r\nOne common case is with a MediaStream where audio may have started transmitting but no video frame has been received yet, and may not get there for a while (such as commonly occur with webrtc)\r\nYou don’t want the readyState to be stuck there as playback must start. \r\n\r\nBut @karlt here is referring to the definition of the frame size itself. ",
